# GroundTruth-KB — Goose Manual Session Guide (.goosehints)

Goose is a first-class GroundTruth-KB (GT-KB) coding harness (harness identity G),
a manual peer to Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, and Antigravity for Prime Builder and
Loyal Opposition work. This file orients a manual Goose Desktop / goose CLI session;
the authoritative governance lives in the files it points to.

## Project root boundary
All active GT-KB work stays within E:\GT-KB. GT-KB application files stay within
E:\GT-KB\applications\ (Agent Red at E:\GT-KB\applications\Agent_Red\). No exceptions.

## Session role — start here
Declare your role on the FIRST line of your first message, then open an activity:
- `::init gtkb pb`  → Prime Builder (proposes changes, writes code + spec-derived tests, files implementation reports)
- `::init gtkb lo`  → Loyal Opposition (reviews: writes GO / NO-GO / VERIFIED verdicts)
- then: `::open build` | `::open test` | `::open project` | `::open deliberation` | `::open spec` | `::open ops`
Your session role comes ONLY from this explicit declaration — NEVER from the
TAFE/dispatcher registry configuration (DCL-SESSION-ROLE-RESOLUTION-001 v7).

## Load this governance at session start
- `AGENTS.md` (root) — GT-KB operating contract (Goose reads this hierarchically).
- `.claude/rules/canonical-terminology.md` — glossary.
- `.claude/rules/file-bridge-protocol.md` — Prime Builder ↔ Loyal Opposition bridge.
- `.claude/rules/operating-model.md` — operating model.
- `.claude/rules/prime-builder-role.md`, `.claude/rules/loyal-opposition.md` — role contracts.

## Skills
GT-KB workflow guides live in `.goose/skills/gtkb-*/SKILL.md` (bridge, propose, verify,
work-item, spec, decision-capture, projects, harness-parity-review, session-wrap, and
~30 more). Read the relevant SKILL.md before running the corresponding workflow.

## Bridge protocol — the core workflow
No implementation lands without Loyal Opposition review:
propose → GO → implement → report → VERIFIED, recorded as versioned files under `bridge/`.
Prime Builder acts on GO / NO-GO; Loyal Opposition acts on NEW / REVISED / NO-ACTION.
Read `.goose/skills/gtkb-bridge/SKILL.md` for the mechanics.

## CLI + Python
- `gt` CLI: `gt backlog list`, `gt bridge state-report`, `gt deliberations search "<q>"`,
  `gt projects list`, `gt harness roles`.
- Project Python (imports `groundtruth_kb` without PYTHONPATH):
  `groundtruth-kb/.venv/Scripts/python.exe`
- Canonical knowledge lives in MemBase (`groundtruth.db`) via the `gt` CLI /
  `groundtruth_kb` API — never hand-edit the SQLite file.

## Owner decisions
Collect owner decisions explicitly and record them (see `.goose/skills/gtkb-decision-capture`).
Do not infer approval from context.

